          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em relativistic particle
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is a model for the dynamics of a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} particle
            that is propagating in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            subject to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            and (if it is charged) the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
          %p
            The generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong relativistic particle
            is described by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
              %p
                where the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                – or rather the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+connection"} Levi-Civita connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                that it induces on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
                – encodes the background field of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
                acting on the particle;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = \mathbb{R}
                or the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma = S^1
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline"} worldline
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
                acting by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+force"} Lorentz force
                on the particle;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Conf
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Diff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Conf := C^\infty(\Sigma, X)// Diff(\Sigma)
              %p
                of the space (naturally a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
                (“trajectories”);
            %li
              %p
                the exponentiated
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                is for given parameters
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \in \mathbb{R}
                (the particle’s
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \in \mathbb{R}
                (the particle’s
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi dvol
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi γ
                        %mo *
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi hol
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo ,
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\exp(i S(-))
                      \:
                      [\gamma]
                      \\mapsto
                      \\exp(
                      i m \int dvol(\gamma^* g))
                      \\;\;
                      hol(\nabla,\gamma)
                      \\,,
              %p
                where the first terms is the integral of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
                of the pullback of the background metric, and where the second term is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle bundle with connection
                around
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
                is trivial, so that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
                is given by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} 1-form
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(X)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi S
                              %mo :
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi S
                                %mi kin
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo +
                              %msub
                                %mi S
                                %mi gauge
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo =
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi m
                              %mi dvol
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msup
                                %mi γ
                                %mo *
                              %mi g
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo +
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi q
                              %msup
                                %mi γ
                                %mo *
                              %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\begin{aligned}
                      S :
                      [\gamma]
                      \\mapsto
                      \&amp;
                      S_{kin}([\gamma]) + S_{gauge}([\gamma])
                      \\\
                      \&amp; =
                      \\int m dvol(\gamma^* g)
                      +
                      \\int q \gamma^* A
                      \\end{aligned}
                      \\,,
              %p
                where the first summand is the
                %em kinetic action
                and the second the
                %em gauge interaction
                term.
          %p
            The above action functional is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            in dimension 1. Alternatively (and mandatorily for vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            parameter), the kinetic action is replaced by the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#covariant_phase_space Covariant phase space
          %p
            We determine the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of the theory: the space of solutions to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
          %p
            We assume for simplicity that the class of the background circle bundle is trivial, so that the connection is equivalently given by a 1-form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in \Omega^1(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = d A
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variation
              of the gauge interaction term is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Σ
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mo *
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo ˙
                    %mo ,
                    %mi δ
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta \int_\Sigma \gamma^* A
                    \=
                    \- \int_\Sigma F(\dot \gamma, \delta \gamma)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^d \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} U \hookrightarrow X
              be a local
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+patch"} coordinate patch
              with coordinates
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^\mu\}
              and assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              takes values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              (or at least that its variation is supported there, which we can assume without restriction of generality). Then the variation is given by is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
